    "lawCode": "Amd §398-d, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S516A\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to requiring\nmotor vehicle repair shops to disclose certain information to customers\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to increase the transparency between an auto-\nmotive customer and an auto repair shop regarding the costs of car work\nand repairs.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends subdivisions 1 and 2 of section 398-d of\nthe vehicle and traffic law, subdivision 1 amends chapter 161 of the\nlaws of 1996 and subdivision 2 amends chapter 161 of the laws of 1990\nand adds new subdivision 2-a.\n\nSection2 of the bill provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe maintenance of one's car is costly, vet necessary to keep not only\noneself safe, but also the drivers around us safe as well. In order for\nautomotive owners to be informed of the costs and warranty purchased for\ncar maintenance, it is necessary that they be given a clear record of\nthe costs of the service they get. A motor vehicle repair shop must\nmaintain the upmost clear communication with the owner of a vehicle that\nis being prepared.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023/2024: S2378 Referred to Transportation\n\n2022: S9257 Referred to Transportation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone noted.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
