    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §398-d, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S516B\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to requiring\nmotor vehicle repair shops to disclose certain information to customers\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to increase transparency between an automo-\ntive customer and an auto repair shop by requiring shops to clearly\nstate on invoices to customers what their shop warranties are on parts\nand/or labor.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends subdivisions 1 and 2 of section 398-d of\nthe vehicle and traffic law, subdivision 1 amends chapter 161 of the\nlaws of 1996 and subdivision 2 amends chapter 161 of the laws of 1990\nand adds new subdivision 2-a.\n\nSection 2 of the bill provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation strengthens consumer protections by requiring motor\nvehicle repair shops to clearly disclose whether replacement parts\nand/or labor are covered by a shop warranty. The bill also establishes\npenalties for noncompliance in the form of escalating fines for each\nviolation.\n\nBy increasing transparency between motor vehicle repair shops and their\ncustomers, this legislation ensure that consumers have clear information\nabout repair shop warranties on parts and/or labor while promoting\naccountability and fair business practices across New York's automotive\nrepair industry.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2025: S516A Referred to Transportation and advanced to Third Reading\n\n2023/2024: S2378 Referred to Transportation\n\n2022: S9257 Referred to Transportation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone noted.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
